 support, and valuable insights to facilitate the healing process.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs32\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Understanding Stroke}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 

\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 - Defining stroke and its impact on individuals and families
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
Stroke - A stroke is a serious medical condition that occurs when the blood supply to a part of the brain is interrupted or reduced. This deprives brain tissue of essential nutrients and oxygen, leading to the death of brain cells within minutes. The effe
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 cts of a stroke depend on the part of the brain that was affected and the amount of damage done. Symptoms c\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
an include sudden numbness or weakness, especially on one side of the body, confusion, trouble speaking or understanding speech, difficulty seeing, dizziness, loss of balance, and severe headache.
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 There are primarily three types of strokes:
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 1.\tab Ischemic Stroke: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
This is the most common type of stroke, accounting for about 85% of all cases. It happens when a blood clot obstructs the flow of blood to the brain. The clot may form in an artery that\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
s already very narrow, or it can form somewhere else in the body\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37  and travel to the brain.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 2.\tab Hemorrhagic Stroke: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
This type of stroke occurs when a blood vessel in the brain ruptures or leaks. This leakage of blood can put pressure on brain cells and damage them. Hemorrhagic strokes are less common but tend to be more deadly.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 3.\tab Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 \hich\f37 Also known as a \'93\loch\f37 \hich\f37 mini-stroke,\'94\loch\f37  a TIA is a temporary period of symptoms similar to those of a stroke. A TIA doesn
\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 t cause permanent damage and is often caused by a temporary decrease in blood supply to part of the \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 brain.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Types of Ischemic Strokes}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 1.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn 
\pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec\pnf37\pnstart1 {\pntxta .}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid5317121 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
Thrombotic Stroke: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
This type of stroke occurs when a blood clot (thrombus) forms in one of the arteries that supply blood to the brain. The clot may be caused by fatty deposits (plaque) that build up in arteries and cause reduced blood flow, or atherosclerosis.
