\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs28\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Understanding the Phases of Stroke\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37  Recovery}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Recovering from a stroke is a journey that unfolds in several stages. Each individual\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
s path to recovery will be unique, influenced by the severity of the stroke, the specific area of the brain affected, their overall health, and the rehabilitation method\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
s used. However, most stroke survivors will progress through three primary phases of recovery: acute, subacute, and long-term.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Acute Phase}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 
