\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 My foray into the world of TikTok was rather unex\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
pected. I used to tease my wife about her endless scrolling through videos until a thought struck me. Why not leverage this platform to document my recovery journey? Thus, I began recording videos on my phone.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
My first video was a testimonial, a brief recount of my stroke experience, the challenges I faced, and my ongoing recovery process. It was a two-minute clip that set the stage for my TikTok journey. Following this, I posted a 30-second video of myself per
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 forming exercises.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 The response was immediate\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
 and overwhelming. Followers started pouring in, and I received numerous comments about how my journey was inspiring hope in other survivors. This realization sparked an idea - by sharing my recovery journey on TikTok, I could inspire others while also mo
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 tivating myself. It was a win-win situation.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 As I continued to create videos, my follower count surged. Upon reaching a thousand followers, TikTok granted me the ability to go live. I seized this opportunity to interact with other survivors, answering thei
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 r questions and sharing experiences. This interaction solidified my decision to fully commit to being a digital creator.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
With each video I posted, my follower count grew. Upon reaching 10,000 followers, TikTok invited me to join their creator beta program, which offered payment for each video. This development sparked a desire in me to either return to school to become a th
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 erapist or use my recovery experience to become a life coach.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Motivated by this, I decided to create a nonprofit, website and social s\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
pace for recovering stroke survivors called Stroke Lyfe Inc. at StrokeLyfe.com.The mission at Stroke Lyfe Inc is to hassist financially strugglig families in the aftermath of a stroke as well as help stroke survivors gain their independence by helping the
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
m modify their veicle to drive.I then filled out the paperwork and paid to make it official.  Then I filled out a form to make Stroke Lyfe Inc, a public, tax exempt, charity. I began designing and selling t-shirts, and also started dropshipping stroke rec
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 ov\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
ery tools to my fellow survivors. However, this venture turned out to be quite a disaster. I invested about five thousand dollars in setting up the site on Shopify and hiring professional digital creators for SEO optimization. Unfortunately, I ended up ac
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 cidentally dropshipping an Apple watch to someone using a stolen credit card, which resulted in nearly a thousand dollars in charges. A costly lesson learned!
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Since then, I\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 ve discontinued the watch sales business and launched StrokeLyfe.org. This platform\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
 offers a social community featuring shared blogs, a message board, and of course, dropshipping of stroke recovery tools. I\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 m hopeful that this venture will be successful!
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs32\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 How I got my arm back
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
Regaining the use of my arm was an entirely different challenge. It all began with my shoulder, where I started with simple shrugs. The key to stroke recovery, I found, was consistency, persistence, experimentation, and working with whatever the stroke al
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 lowed. It was all about taking small steps and focusing on mak\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 ing a little progress each day, all while exercising extreme patience.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
As I mentioned, my recovery started in my shoulder and gradually worked its way down to my tricep, bicep, and now my forearm and fingers. As my arm improved, I pushed myself and expanded my exercises. I would sit in my old wheelchair and practice lifting 
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 my arm over and over again, even while on the toilet! I discovered that as long as negative pressure was applied, the muscle would respond.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 My caretaker, Karlie, was instrumental in th\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
is process. She would wrap an elastic band around my wrist, and we would practice lifting in every conceivable way - shoulder presses, bicep curls, tricep extensions, chest presses, and even wrapping the band around my foot to work on drop foot. I can
\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 t s\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
tress enough the importance of fully utilizing your caretaker. They can provide connection and care in numerous ways. Karlie was incredible. She even went above and beyond her duties to cut my nails and shave me from head to toe, even in the most private 
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 ar\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 eas!
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
Following this, I began making TikTok videos of myself lifting elastic bands with handles, which proved to be highly effective. I would lean onto the kitchen island and practice tricep extensions and pushup leans. I was then ready to attempt a pushup, but
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37  there was a problem; I had no strength in my hand yet. I couldn\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
t place my hand flat on the ground with weight because it would curl up. I purchased push-up bars from Temu and decided to give it a try. I found I could grip the bar quite tightly, but \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 couldn\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
t release it. I filmed myself attempting a pushup. I managed to lower myself almost to my nose, then push back up. I did it! I decided to try another one, but failed and fell flat on my face. However, I had managed to do one! I then practiced these
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37  every day and eventually got to where I could do twenty in a row.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 My hand was the most challenging part because it required fine motor skills, and the hand and forearm have so many different nerves to reconnect. I purchased a hemiplegia hand robotic train\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
ing glove for one hundred and fifty dollars. It used pneumatic pressure to manually open and close my hand, hopefully forging new connections in the process. I would use it daily with my eyes closed, focusing on making new connections. After a few months 
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 of not seeing much progress, I sold it.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 I then decided to try baseball bat therapy. I would grip the baseball bat and practice lifting it over my head and back again, working my shoulder and forearm. I then progressed to moving the weight of the baseball b
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 at back and forth, working my wrist and forearm. This journey has been a testament to the power of persistence, patience, and the human spirit.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs32\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Outpatient Therapy
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
During a follow-up visit for my stroke recovery, I met with my neurologist. She was genuinely impressed by the progress I had made thus far. So much so, she felt there was no longer a need for me to continue seeing her. However, when she asked if I wanted
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37  more therapy, I didn\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 t hesitate to say yes.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 I proceeded to attend local outpatient therapy. \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
Here, they tested me in various areas, including walking with my eyes closed, looking up, down, side to side, side steps, and other coordination exercises. It was during these sessions that I discovered the use of wedges. These devices allowed me to stret
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 ch my leg and work towards completely overcoming my drop foot. I was so convinced of their effectiveness that I bought a pair for myself!
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 I also incorporated cycling on an exercise bike into my routine. However, despite my efforts, the physical therapist i\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
nformed me that I still needed to wear an Ankle Foot Orthosis (AFO). This news was disheartening, considering the hard work I had put into avoiding it.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
In occupational therapy, I engaged in a variety of exercises. I practiced squeezing a pressure gauge and spent time with a weighted wrist strap and stick, doing stretches, chest presses, and working on the hand bike. I also performed chest stretches in a 
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 corner with my arms raised, in a desperate attempt to regain the use of my arm.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 This journey has been f\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
illed with ups and downs, but each step, no matter how small, brings me closer to recovery. The road may be long and challenging, but I am committed to seeing it through. After all, it\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
s not just about getting back on my feet; it\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 s about reclaiming my lif\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 e. And I won\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 t stop until I\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 ve done just that.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\fs32\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Conclusion}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\fs22\lang9\langfe1033\kerning0\langnp9\insrsid10578587 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 As we conclude, let\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
s reflect on the journey so far. Today, I continue to create TikTok videos as part of my recovery process, serving as a beacon of hope for fellow stroke survivors. I have regained\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
 my ability to walk, albeit with a slight limp. I can even manage short bursts of jogging, despite my Physical Therapist\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 s advice against it.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
Stroke recovery is not a journey for the weak-willed. It is a marathon, not a sprint, requiring patience, resilience, and determination. However, with the right mindset, no obstacle is insurmountable. The secret lies in maintaining a positive attitude and
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37  the motivation to engage in daily exercises. It\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 s crucial to rise, get your blood circulating, and commit to at l\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
east a small amount of physical activity each day.Consider starting a vlog and sharing your progress on social media. This not only inspires other survivors but also creates a sense of accountability for your own exercise regimen. This has been my strateg
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 y so far, and it\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 s one I plan to stick with.
\par 
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Remember, things do get better, but the change starts with you. I have faith in your ability to overcome this, but the real question is, do you believe in yourself? Best of luck on your journey, fellow stroke wa
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 rriors!
